show with animations:
   lives at underpaint.brianmeier.dev: a solid page in site/, built by npm run build:site, published with vercel once the three scenes play
   each animation is the real Editor, read-only, playing a scripted session when you scroll to it and pausing when you scroll away
   it imports app/style.css, so colours, margin marks and light or dark are the editor's own
   scenes reuse what the editor already has (Editor, Underneath, edit, fromReply), nothing copied

   if (coding is slow but fun):
       you can prompt with code
       a pseudocode line types itself, the margin mark goes from needs-a-build to built, and real code slides in underneath

   when code gets complicated:
      abstractions get created for you
      three settled lines fold into a named box and leave a one-line reference behind
   when agents have questions:
      they ask
      a question appears right under the line it is about, the person types an answer, the waiting-on-a-question mark clears
